From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Glathe <jens.glathe@oldschoolsolutions.biz>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 10:56:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: mux: ps883x: handle DP pin F and wait after
 config writes

Backport of two changes from the jglathe/linux_ms_dev_kit branch
jg/ubuntu-qcom-x1e-7.3rc (commits 42f1fda6edc3 and 40fe9c901381,
September 2026), squashed and rebased onto Fedora 7.2.9-300:

- Several docks (e.g. Lenovo 40B0, SSK SC220) still request the legacy
  TYPEC_DP_STATE_F (DP + USB3). qcom-qmp-combo already treats it like
  pin D; do the same in the retimer instead of leaving the DP lanes
  unconfigured.
- Give the retimer 30 ms after writing the connection-status registers
  so DP Alt Mode hotplug is reliable.

Signed-off-by: Jens Glathe <jens.glathe@oldschoolsolutions.biz>
[Kacper Goc: squashed and rebased onto Fedora 7.2.9-300 for ASUS Vivobook S15]
---
 drivers/usb/typec/mux/ps883x.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/mux/ps883x.c b/drivers/usb/typec/mux/ps883x.c
index 64e0a61b7..ee75eabb2 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/mux/ps883x.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/mux/ps883x.c
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 
 #include <drm/bridge/aux-bridge.h>
 #include <linux/clk.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/gpio/consumer.h>
 #include <linux/i2c.h>
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
@@ -184,6 +185,14 @@ static int ps883x_configure(struct ps883x_retimer *retimer, int cfg0,
 		return ret;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The retimer needs time after the connection-status registers are
+	 * written for the analog front-end (PLLs, lane training) to settle.
+	 * Without this, DisplayPort Alt Mode hotplug is unreliable on some
+	 * docks (e.g. Lenovo 40B0).
+	 */
+	fsleep(30000);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
@@ -207,6 +216,7 @@ static int ps883x_set(struct ps883x_retimer *retimer, struct typec_retimer_state
 
 			switch (state->mode)  {
 			case TYPEC_DP_STATE_D:
+			case TYPEC_DP_STATE_F:
 				cfg0 |= CONN_STATUS_0_USB_3_1_CONNECTED;
 				fallthrough;
 			case TYPEC_DP_STATE_C:
